  "releaseNotes": "Security fix: sensitive HTTP headers are now redacted in diagnostic output.\n\n      Previously AuthenticatedHttpClientHandler passed the whole HttpRequestMessage to the logger,\n      and its ToString() renders every header. The X-Auth-Token set on each request was therefore\n      written verbatim, on every attempt of the retry loop. The response side did the same.\n\n      This also exposed the account credentials, not only the session token. The token endpoint is\n      called with an Authorization header carrying Basic encoded username and password, and that\n      request travels through the same handler.\n\n      X-Auth-Token, Authorization, Proxy-Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie and common API key\n      headers are now redacted, case-insensitively, on request and response. The scheme and\n      credential length are retained, so failures remain diagnosable.\n\n      Breaking change to message text: the Request and Response log messages are now rendered by\n      this library rather than by HttpRequestMessage.ToString(). The shape is the same but code\n      parsing those messages should be checked.\n\n      Consumers should upgrade, review existing Trace logs for previously captured credentials, and\n      change any password that appears in them.\n\n      Also in this release: more Options to support query retries with backoff, plus better logging\n      of status codes.",
